Source: agent-shell
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Agent Shell <agent-shell@example.com>
Build-Depends: cargo, libpipewire-0.3-dev | libpipewire-dev, pkg-config, libsystemd-dev
Standards-Version: 4.6.0

Package: agent-shell
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends: systemd, xdg-desktop-portal, pipewire
Description: Agent Shell — Linux desktop agent shell
 Agent Shell is a desktop automation framework providing window management,
 input injection, screenshot capture, and accessibility integration across
 KDE, GNOME, DDE, Hyprland, Sway, and X11.
 .
 This package contains the user-session daemon (agent-shell-daemon), CLI
 (agent-shell), and MCP server (agent-shell-mcp).
 .
 systemd user service: agent-shell-daemon.service (graphical-session.target).
 .
 udev rules: 60-agent-shell-uinput.rules grants /dev/uinput to the `uinput`
 group for ydotool input injection fallback (§20.3 权限模型).

Package: agent-shell-rootd
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends: policykit-1, systemd
Description: Agent Shell rootd — privileged proxy (systemd system unit)
 Agent Shell rootd is the privileged proxy daemon (§23.2/§23.4): a thin
 stateless agent exposing a whitelisted D-Bus interface on the system bus,
 with per-method polkit authorization (auth_admin_keep).
 .
 This package contains:
   * agent-shell-rootd binary (systemd system unit, system-level singleton)
   * /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/com.agentshell.policy
   * /usr/lib/agent-shell/rootd-pkexec (pkexec fallback, §23.4.1 channel 3)
 .
 rootd is independently installable — when absent, privileged operations
 return "rootd not installed" and degrade to user-only operations (§23.2).
